From f733425c5faaaf74cb64ce601aae792613ca67d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:38:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dsv41(tilelang): remove fused mHC entry optionality for
 2-launch PDL

Upstream base: 09963f65c537e6d153e12f9fb08b22ffbc721258
Rationale: Two-launch project_streams + finalize on GB10 (48 SMs) uses the 8
  idle SMs during M=1 projection (40 split CTAs) to preload weight, scale, and
  base in finalize before pdl.chain(), executing in 8.71-8.81 us versus
  13.06-13.86 us for fused project_and_finalize_streams (-4.3..-5.1 us/call,
  -345..-410 us per 40-layer forward pass at M=1) and winning at every M >= 1.
  Remove project_and_finalize_streams, FINALIZE_FUSE_MAX_ROWS, _FUSE_HEADER,
  and split arrival counters so mHC sublayer entry unconditionally dispatches
  the faster two-launch path and skips eight redundant JIT compilations.
Quality implications: None. Bit-identical FP32/BF16/MXFP8 outputs across all
  token counts, modes, and non-finite inputs.
Tests: pytest tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_mhc.py (174 passed).
Upstream status: Local to DeepSeek-V4.1 SM120/SM121 TileLang integration.
